 Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- You have taken a radar processing chain from raw ADC data to detections on real hardware, not only in simulation.&lt;br&gt;- Deep understanding of radar signal processing â€” range-Doppler processing, direction-of-arrival estimation, detection theory, clutter â€” and of the underlying radar physics.&lt;br&gt;- Strong C++ for real-time systems; Python or MATLAB for prototyping and analysis.&lt;br&gt;- Master&#39;s degree or PhD in Electrical Engineering, Communications Engineering, Physics or a comparable field.&lt;br&gt;- Fluent English; German is a plus.&lt;br&gt;- Citizenship of a NATO member state.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- MIMO radar and array processing&lt;br&gt;- Radar on moving platforms, including ego-motion compensation&lt;br&gt;- Embedded acceleration (GPU, SIMD, FPGA)&lt;br&gt;- Learning-based radar detection or classification&lt;br&gt;- ROS2 and experience with field testing&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relevant Backgrounds&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Deep expertise in radar signal processing matters more to us than meeting every single requirement. You might come from automotive radar and ADAS, aerospace or defence radar, telecommunications and SDR, or academic radar research.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why STARK&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;- Impact: Your work directly strengthens the autonomy of STARK systems and the technological edge of European defence.&lt;br&gt;- Innovation: Work in a builder culture where you take radar sensing from first concept to field deployment.&lt;br&gt;- Growth: Shape how STARK uses radar from the ground up and grow with the capability.&lt;br&gt;- Collaboration: Join a multi-national team of navigation, perception, radar and test engineers where practical solutions count.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline; font-size: 10pt; font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Equal Opportunity:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
